    },
    {
      "data": {
        "type": "step-start"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc29a55f001JUbJW2okce9vIj",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc29a0db0013XBoxop5zNxc3u",
      "session_id": "ses_f43d65f35ffeYea2y0UqVo4O8s",
      "time_created": 1789863241055,
      "time_updated": 1789863241056
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Provider**\n\nI'm currently focused on the implementation details for `embed_batch.py`. I've settled on OpenAI as the embedding provider and will be utilizing their official Python client. The code will explicitly reference OpenAI for clarity and future maintainability. My next step involves integrating the client into the core logic.\n\n\n**Outlining the Implementation**\n\nI've got the initial structure of `embed_batch.py` sketched out. The plan is to import the OpenAI library and create a function, `generate_embeddings_batch`, which takes text as input. I'll use `openai.Embedding.create` to generate those embeddings and include the model name within the function so that I'm clear on the logic. The goal is maintainability and clarity.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863242622,
          "start": 1789863241057
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc29a561001YdVQ3Cwe2E43ih",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc29a0db0013XBoxop5zNxc3u",
      "session_id": "ses_f43d65f35ffeYea2y0UqVo4O8s",
      "time_created": 1789863241057,
      "time_updated": 1789863242623
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "wRHH4KBxoAggnHUM",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nimport os\nimport openai\n\ndef generate_embeddings_batch(texts: list[str], model: str = \"text-embedding-ada-002\") -> list[list[float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates embeddings for a batch of texts using OpenAI's embedding model.\n\n    Args:\n        texts: A list of strings to embed.\n        model: The OpenAI embedding model to use.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of embeddings, where each embedding is a list of floats.\n    \"\"\"\n    openai.api_key = os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")\n    if not openai.api_key:\n        raise ValueError(\"OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable not set.\")\n\n    response = openai.Embedding.create(\n        input=texts,\n        model=model\n    )\n    return [data.embedding for data in response.data]\n",
            "filePath": "embed_batch.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
